# TaskForge 🔧

> **Open-Source, Production-Grade DevOps Task Scheduler & Web Dashboard**
>
> Cron jobs, interval tasks, webhook triggers, event-driven pipelines, streaming logs, and real-time execution monitoring — all managed through a sleek Web Dashboard, clean REST API, and powerful CLI.

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
[![Python 3.11+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11%2B-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![FastAPI](https://img.shields.io/badge/FastAPI-0.110%2B-009688.svg)](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com)
[![APScheduler](https://img.shields.io/badge/APScheduler-3.11-orange.svg)](https://github.com/agronholm/apscheduler)
[![Code style: ruff](https://img.shields.io/badge/code%20style-ruff-000000.svg)](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff)

---

## 🖥️ Modern Web UI Dashboard

TaskForge comes equipped with a **single-page admin web dashboard (SPA)** served directly by the backend at `http://localhost:8080/`:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 🔧 TASKFORGE                                          [☀ Light] [🔔] [👤 Admin] │
├───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 📊 Dashboard  │  Total Jobs: 12   │  Active: 9   │  Failed: 1   │  Uptime: 99.9%  │
│ 📋 Jobs       ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 📜 Live Logs  │  Job Runs Activity (Success vs Failed Chart)                │
│ ⚡ Triggers    │  [████████████████████████████████████████████████]         │
│ 🔔 Alerts     ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 📈 Metrics    │  Recent Jobs:                                               │
│ 🔌 Plugins    │  • daily-db-backup    [cron: 0 2 * * *]    [SUCCESS]  [▶] [✏]  │
│ 🛡️ Health     │  • cache-invalidation [every 30m]          [RUNNING]  [▶] [✏]  │
│ ⚙️ Settings   │  • health-check-prod  [every 5m]           [SUCCESS]  [▶] [✏]  │
└───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Dashboard Highlights:
- **9 Dedicated Views**: Dashboard Overview, Jobs Management, Live Execution Logs, Triggers, Notifications, Metrics / Observability, System Health, Plugins Catalog, and System Settings.
- **Instant Interactive Control**: Trigger executions on-demand (`▶`), Pause/Resume schedules (`⏸`/`↺`), inspect live streaming logs (`📋`), and edit configs (`✏`).
- **Visual Analytics**: Interactive 7-day success/failure bar charts and donut charts powered by Chart.js.
- **Theme & Personalization**: Smooth dark / light mode toggle with 5 custom accent color palettes (Blue, Emerald, Purple, Amber, Red).
- **Dual Mode Operation**: Connects live to the TaskForge backend API with automatic fallback to standalone demo mode.

---

## ✨ System Features

| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| 🖥️ **Web Dashboard UI** | Full-featured SPA admin console served directly out of the box |
| 🕐 **Cron Scheduling** | Full 5/6-field standard cron expressions with timezone support |
| ⏱ **Interval Triggers** | Flexible intervals (`every 30m`, `every 1h`, `every 5s`) with jitter |
| 🎯 **One-Shot Jobs** | Fire once at a specific datetime and self-archive |
| 🌐 **Webhook Triggers** | Trigger jobs securely via incoming HTTP POST requests with secret verification |
| 🔗 **Event-Driven Pub/Sub** | Decoupled event bus (`job.started`, `job.success`, `job.failed`) |
| 🐚 **Shell Executor** | Execute CLI/shell commands with real-time stdout/stderr capture |
| 🐍 **Python Callable Executor** | Run dynamic Python code snippets and callables safely |
| 🌍 **HTTP Executor** | Invoke external REST endpoints with custom payloads and methods |
| 🐳 **Docker Executor** | Run jobs inside ephemeral Docker containers (`docker run`) |
| 🔁 **Smart Retry Policies** | Configurable retries with exponential backoff and jitter |
| 🔌 **Plugin Architecture** | Modular extensions (K8s executor, Discord alerts, Git triggers) |
| 📊 **Prometheus Metrics** | Scrape-ready Prometheus exposition at `/metrics` |
| 📖 **OpenAPI / Swagger** | Interactive API documentation at `/docs` |
| 💾 **Backend Storage** | Async SQLite (`aiosqlite`) default with PostgreSQL roadmap |

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

### 1. Clone & Set Up Environment

```bash
git clone https://github.com/mibrahimmustafa/TaskForge_DevOps_Tools.git
cd TaskForge_DevOps_Tools

# Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv .venv

# On Windows PowerShell:
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# On Linux/macOS:
source .venv/bin/activate
```

### 2. Install Dependencies

```bash
# Install core dependencies
pip install fastapi "uvicorn[standard]" apscheduler pydantic \
  sqlalchemy aiosqlite httpx typer rich structlog \
  prometheus-client "python-jose[cryptography]" \
  "passlib[bcrypt]" python-multipart python-dotenv

# Install TaskForge in editable mode (registers the 'taskforge' CLI):
pip install -e .
```

### 3. Configure

```bash
# Copy default environment settings
cp .env.example .env
```

### 4. Start the Server & Web Dashboard

```bash
# Using the TaskForge CLI:
taskforge server start

# Or directly with Uvicorn:
uvicorn taskforge.api.app:create_app --factory --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080 --reload
```

Open your browser to:
- 🌐 **Dashboard UI**: [http://localhost:8080/](http://localhost:8080/)
- 📖 **Interactive API Docs (Swagger)**: [http://localhost:8080/docs](http://localhost:8080/docs)
- 📊 **Prometheus Metrics**: [http://localhost:8080/metrics](http://localhost:8080/metrics)
- 🩺 **Health Check**: [http://localhost:8080/health](http://localhost:8080/health)

---

## 💻 CLI Commands

```bash
# Check version
taskforge version

# Start server
taskforge server start --port 8080

# List configured jobs
taskforge jobs list

# Create a job from JSON definition
taskforge jobs create examples/hello_world_job.json

# Run a job immediately
taskforge jobs run job-hello-world
```

---

## 📋 Example Job Definition

```json
{
  "id": "job-hello-world",
  "name": "hello-world",
  "description": "Simple hello world demonstration job",
  "trigger": "interval",
  "trigger_expr": "every 1m",
  "executor": "shell",
  "command": "echo 'Hello from TaskForge!'",
  "status": "active",
  "tags": ["demo", "getting-started"],
  "timeout_seconds": 300,
  "max_retries": 3,
  "retry_delay_seconds": 5
}
```

